    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To both parties. This is the metered trip TRP-05005 of 15 Aug 2026 from Waterway Point, Punggol Central to Paya Lebar Quarter. The platform's own recorded distances — which POL-RD-22 (v2.1 1.3-1.4) makes the measure, not the sparse trace — are 13.8 km actually driven against a 12.1 km recommended route, a deviation of 1.70 km. That is above the 1.0 km tolerance, so a refundable deviation over tolerance is established (POL-RD-22). Driver: after the TPE / Upper Serangoon Road exit was taken at 10:21:30 the vehicle ran Upper Serangoon Road and Upper Paya Lebar Road, rejoining at Paya Lebar Road / Upper Paya Lebar Road at 10:35:21. POL-RD-21 requires you to inform the rider of the deviation before or at the point of deviation. You messaged at 10:24:30 — about 3 minutes afterwards — and the record carries no trip call recording, so the notice was late in time and the late notice cannot be read as a validly agreed reroute. The rider's 'ok noted' at 10:25:00 (MSG-05005-004) answered a message written in the past tense about a reroute already under way; it acknowledges a fact, it does not cure the earlier breach. Row (a) of POL-RD-24 (no refund) therefore does not apply. The traffic question does not change this: the LTA advisory EV-ADVIS-05005-01 (a VEHICLE_BREAKDOWN on the KPE towards ECP, valid 09:59:38-10:54:38, overlapping the trip) may or may not intersect the recommended route, and POL-RD-23 leaves that determination to the Judge; but if it justifies the reroute row (b) applies, and if it does not row (d) applies, and both rows refund the excess distance fare in full. Rider: your request for 5.00 SGD exceeds what the policy provides. POL-RD-24 pays only the excess distance fare, and it is 1.70 km x 0.92 SGD per km (base rate, no surge) = 1.56 SGD, rounded to the cent and carried in the fare breakdown EV-FARE-05005. You were charged 23.04 SGD with refund_issued_sgd 0.0, so 1.56 SGD of that charge is returned to you and the balance stands. The AI is permitted to decide this case: the deviation of 1.70 km is within POL-RD-25's 2 km ceiling, the contested 5.00 SGD is below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD band so the AI ruling is final, neither profile carries a fraud flag, and there is no safety indicator anywhere in the record. The evidence bundle is complete and every artifact carries weight 1.0, so confidence sits above the 0.80 POL-RD-25 requires. Figures used: actual 13.8 km, optimal 12.1 km, deviation 1.70 km, tolerance 1.0 km, per-km rate 0.92 SGD, excess distance fare 1.56 SGD, contested amount 5.00 SGD, AI deviation ceiling 2.0 km, required confidence 0.80.",
    "referrals": []
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

